I think the easiest thing would be to make the new version of g++ the system default.

Otherwise, see

http://cran.r-project.org/doc/manuals/R-admin.html#Customizing-package-compilation

> Question 2
> ----------
> How do I work with R when developing packages so
> that I can uninstall and reinstall a package without
> quitting R?

I have never seen loading, unloading, and reloading a package work well, except if the R code is very simple and there is no compiled code.

If you just need to test modified R code, you can usually just paste it into the R session. But if you modify source code, it is easiest to quit R, reinstall the package, and restart R.

Ben

