Perhaps more worrisome is the fact that CRAN currently uses GCC 4.2.1 to build binary packages. See

http://cran.r-project.org/web/checks/check_flavors.html#r-release-macosx-ix86

So, if 4.2.1 is not good enough, then there won't be Mac binary for the *stan package. At that point, users would have to install the package from source and they would have to have a proper toolchain.

Looks to me like fallback is unavoidable for the time being.

