We should cut out the loops since they are equivalent to

log_prob += log_sds.sum() * K * 2.0;

but the Jacobian (sub)matrix is diagonal of order K choose 2. The diagonal has the product of every pair of standard deviations because the the derivative of the i,j covariance with respect to the i,j correlation is the product of the ith and jth standard deviation.

