>
>     C = (A * A) * B; // FAIL
>
>     The problem is that A.transpose() is not of type
>     Matrix<var,Dynamic,Dynamic>, nor is (A * A). They
>     each have their own expression template type that's
>     only related to the base type through the curiously
>     recursive template pattern. So you need to keep
>     implementing for all of these expression templates.
>
> Assuming we resolve the compiler errors that we haven't been able to
> resolve for months, would it work if we littered the C++ code with
> .eval() as described in
>
> http://eigen.tuxfamily.org/dox/TopicLazyEvaluation.html
>
> Like
>
> C = A.transpose().eval() * B; // FAIL?
>
> C = (A * A).eval() * B; // FAIL?
>
> Ben
