I've pushed changes which add a maximum tree depth to NUTS.  It defaults
 to 10 and can be set from the command line of a generated model program
 by passing --max_treedepth.  Setting it to -1 will fall back to the previous behavior which does not limit the depth of the tree.

I haven't added a diagnostic to check how often this is hit but I pushed the changes anyway in case someone else has the time and motivation to do that.

Cheers,
Marcus

