On 3/26/12 6:46 PM, Matt Hoffman wrote:
> Hmm. Maybe a solution to vectorization is to encourage people do
> everything with eigen vectors (two words!), a la Matlab/R/python. Not
> that I necessarily think we should rewrite Matlab, but there's
> certainly something to be said for that sort of compact notation and
> the easy optimization it enables.

In order for that to work, there need to be vectorized
versions of the functions to call.

We could try to do this kind of thing automatically in
the Stan Modeling Language compiler, where if we have
a function

    double foo(double);

automatically extend it elementwise to:

    matrix foo(matrix);

But we don't really want

   vector normal_log(vector,double,double);

to be automatically derived from

   double normal_log(double,double,double);

Instead, we want to sum the result to get a
double back.

- Bob

