On Monday, March 26, 2012 6:47:08 PM UTC-4, Bob Carpenter wrote:
> There are many ways to do this.

Motion: Use an Eigen Array with a column for the partial and a column for the adjoint so the derivative is something like foo.rowwise.prod().sum().

Question: How would the proposed design generalize to Hessians? In the old design, I thought it was approximately just a matter of making the derivatives into vars and differentiating them again.

But, in general, I would say implement first (in a branch), ask questions later. If you do it and it turns out to be 1% faster, then I am basically sold.

Ben

