A quick note on the Hessian/vector products—it's actually just a
generalization of the scheme that you're suggesting for computing the
Hessians row-wise. The difference is that instead of projecting the
gradient onto an indicator vector you're projecting it into an
arbitrary vector. But the cost is essentially the same—in finite
differences terminology, you're just allowing a bigger space of
perturbations.

Matt

