MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

As long as we can choose the models, we'll do fine.
Seriously, though, these models all run pretty fast.
If those timings are seconds, the worst is under
4 minutes.

That was JAGS vs. OpenBUGS.  1.5 years ago.  Presumably
on a single chain.  To 1000 ESS evaluated by CODA.

To emphasize Matt's point about universality, look at the
comparison of GLM vs. non-GLM for JAGS itself.  RATS
is almost twice as slow with the GLM module on, whereas
some examples are over twice as fast with it on.

- Bob

