Some rare good news on the compiler front. I sullied my otherwise mostly pure laptop by installing the closed source but free-as-in-beer-for-noncommercial-use-iff-you-register-so-we-can-later-attempt-to-sell-you-stuff-you-do-not-want Intel C++ compiler from

http://software.intel.com/en-us/articles/non-commercial-software-download/

This compiler is popular in certain circles. And make test-all (eventually) passes all tests with 55MB of warnings output, most of which are repetitive and pertain to Eigen or boost rather than stan specifically. The only useful stuff I could grep in the warnings was

goodrich@CYBERPOWERPC:/tmp$ grep "^src" warnings.txt
src/test/prob/distributions/multivariate/continuous/lkj_corr_test.cpp(59): warning #265: floating-point operation result is out of range
src/test/prob/distributions/multivariate/continuous/lkj_cov_test.cpp(59): warning #265: floating-point operation result is out of range
src/stan/math/error_handling.hpp(460): warning #186: pointless comparison of unsigned integer with zero
src/stan/math/error_handling.hpp(460): warning #186: pointless comparison of unsigned integer with zero
src/stan/math/error_handling.hpp(460): warning #186: pointless comparison of unsigned integer with zero
src/test/math/matrix_test.cpp(194): warning #68: integer conversion resulted in a change of sign
src/test/math/matrix_test.cpp(194): warning #68: integer conversion resulted in a change of sign
src/test/math/matrix_test.cpp(197): warning #68: integer conversion resulted in a change of sign
src/test/math/matrix_test.cpp(198): warning #68: integer conversion resulted in a change of sign
src/test/math/matrix_test.cpp(200): warning #68: integer conversion resulted in a change of sign
src/test/math/matrix_test.cpp(200): warning #68: integer conversion resulted in a change of sign

Perhaps we should make it a habit of occasionally testing stan with Intel's C++ compiler and / or mention that it is as supported as recent versions of clang are?

Ben

