On Saturday, March 31, 2012 6:51:22 PM UTC-4, Jiqiang Guo wrote:
> I should have said that I could help test building on windows.  I have windows 7 64bits and windows xp 32 bits.  But I guess the issue to me is that there is not a shell on which `make` could run as on Unix-like system.

If you install the latest Rtools from

http://cran.r-project.org/bin/windows/Rtools/

it puts the command-line tools (plus a compiler and other stuff) listed here

http://cran.r-project.org/doc/manuals/R-admin.html#The-command-line-tools

on your PATH. So, that should be enough to get you started once you also download git for Windows from

http://git-scm.com/download

Ben

